### 6.3 Database Schema and Data Models

The system employs a polyglot persistence approach, using specialized databases for different data types and access patterns.

#### 6.3.1 Core Data Models

**Farm Entity Model:**
```
Farm {
  id: UUID
  name: String
  location: GeoPoint
  totalArea: Decimal (hectares)
  owner: Reference<User>
  fields: List<Reference<Field>>
  devices: List<Reference<Device>>
  createdAt: Timestamp
  updatedAt: Timestamp
}

Field {
  id: UUID
  farmId: Reference<Farm>
  name: String
  boundary: GeoPolygon
  area: Decimal (hectares)
  soilType: Enum<SoilType>
  slope: Decimal (percentage)
  elevation: Decimal (meters)
  crops: List<Reference<Crop>>
  sensors: List<Reference<Device>>
}

Crop {
  id: UUID
  fieldId: Reference<Field>
  species: String (EPPO code)
  variety: String
  plantingDate: Date
  harvestDate: Date (estimated)
  growthStage: String (BBCH code)
  status: Enum<CropStatus>
  history: List<CropEvent>
}
```

**Device Data Model:**
```
Device {
  id: UUID
  type: Enum<DeviceType>
  model: String
  serialNumber: String
  firmwareVersion: String
  location: GeoPoint
  status: Enum<DeviceStatus>
  batteryLevel: Integer (percentage)
  signalStrength: Integer (dBm)
  lastSeen: Timestamp
  properties: Map<String, Any>
}

Sensor extends Device {
  sensorType: Enum<SensorType>
  measurementTypes: List<Enum<MeasurementType>>
  calibrationDate: Date
  accuracy: Map<MeasurementType, Decimal>
  samplingInterval: Integer (seconds)
}

Actuator extends Device {
  actuatorType: Enum<ActuatorType>
  capabilities: List<Enum<ActuatorCapability>>
  currentState: Map<String, Any>
  safeState: Map<String, Any>
}
```

**Measurement Data Model:**
```
Measurement {
  id: UUID
  deviceId: Reference<Device>
  type: Enum<MeasurementType>
  value: Decimal
  unit: String (UCUM code)
  timestamp: Timestamp
  location: GeoPoint
  quality: Enum<DataQuality>
  metadata: Map<String, Any>
}
```

#### 6.3.2 Database Technologies

**Time-Series Database (InfluxDB):**
* Used for: Sensor readings, device telemetry
* Schema: Measurement name, tags (indexed metadata), fields (values), timestamp
* Retention Policy: Tiered storage with automatic downsampling
* Query Language: Flux for complex time-series analysis

**Geospatial Database (PostgreSQL with PostGIS):**
* Used for: Farm boundaries, field zones, sensor locations
* Key Features: Spatial indexing, geospatial queries, topology operations
* Data Types: Point, LineString, Polygon, MultiPolygon
* Functions: Distance calculations, containment tests, spatial joins

**Document Database (MongoDB):**
* Used for: User profiles, farm configurations, complex nested structures
* Schema: Flexible schema with JSON documents
* Indexing: Compound indexes on frequently queried fields
* Sharding: Farm-based sharding for horizontal scaling

**Graph Database (Neo4j):**
* Used for: Relationship analysis, recommendation engine
* Schema: Nodes (entities) and edges (relationships)
* Query Language: Cypher for graph traversal
* Applications: Crop rotation recommendations, pest spread modeling

